-- title:
--   Local components of a finite adele lie in the lattice almost everywhere
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose underlying set spans $D$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. $\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Lambda)=\top$. Let $x$ be an element of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where the finite adele ring is formed for the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside $\mathbb{Q}$. The assertion is that, in the cofinite filter on the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, for all but finitely many height-one primes $v$ — the $v$-th component of $x$ lies in the local box of $\Lambda$ at $v$. Here the $v$-th component is the image of $x$ under the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f} \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ obtained as the tensor product of the identity of $D$ with evaluation of a finite adele at $v$ into the $v$-adic completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$, and the local box is the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the pure tensors $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring $\mathbb{Z}_v$ of $\mathbb{Q}_v$.
--
--   This is the statement that the local component maps realise $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ inside the restricted product of the $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ with respect to the completions $\Lambda_v$ of a full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice $\Lambda \subset D$. It belongs to the local vocabulary used in the place-by-place analysis of ideles of a quaternion algebra, in particular in results expressing a finite idele as a diagonal element times local factors and in the computation of normed reduced valuations.
